cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "pi-fixed-supply — Pi's total native supply is fixed at 100,000,000,000 π on every observable ledger"
abstract: >-
  A read-only, zero-dependency proof that Pi Mainnet's total native supply is exactly
  100,000,000,000 π on every observable ledger, and that no operation in the network's current
  protocol increases it. The claim is verified by decoding the raw consensus-signed ledger header
  (including the issuance counter, which the public API does not expose), by sweeping the observable
  ledger range for the documented cap, and by cross-checking the API's JSON summary against the
  header it summarises. It proves nothing about circulating supply, allocation, unlock schedules,
  price, or any future protocol change.
type: software
